# Network egress

Which services each command reaches, so a firewall rule, a proxy allowance or a fence can be
set from a list rather than from a failed run. Every row names the service in the open and
what changes behind a fenced index, as [Work behind a fenced index](../how-to/work-behind-a-fenced-index.md)
sets one up. A command not listed under a heading reaches nothing.

## The scenarios

Four things decide what a command reaches, and they combine.

- **Open or fenced.** In the open, packages come from PyPI and interpreters from GitHub. Behind
  the fence, `UV_DEFAULT_INDEX` and `UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_MIRROR` redirect both to Artifactory,
  and the `JFROG_*` variables add one more destination: the token exchange at `JFROG_URL`.
- **Cold or warm.** The first `./workflow.cmd` of any kind syncs the environment from
  `uv.lock`, which fetches every package from the index and, if `.python-version` names an
  interpreter the machine lacks, that interpreter. Once synced, the launcher itself reaches
  nothing; the rows below assume a warm environment and list what the command adds.
- **Laptop or pipeline.** A pipeline job adds the host's own traffic: pulling the deps image,
  fetching actions, pushing a registry. The pipeline sections list those per job.
- **GitLab or GitHub.** The release and docs tasks talk to the host's API, and the pipelines
  pull their images from different places. This project is on {{ git_hosting_service | capitalize }}.

Where a row says *index*, read PyPI (`pypi.org` and `files.pythonhosted.org`) in the open and
`UV_DEFAULT_INDEX` behind the fence. Where it says *interpreters*, read GitHub's
`python-build-standalone` releases in the open and `UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_MIRROR` behind it.
*Artifactory* means the token exchange at `JFROG_URL`, reached only when the fence is set, by
`index.login`, `container.tag` and `release.publish` and nothing else.

## Commands that reach nothing

Formatting, linting, type-checking, complexity, commit-message checks, the test run on the
project's own interpreter, the SBOM, and the hook setup all run on what is already installed.

| Command | Why nothing |
| --- | --- |
| `bootstrap` | `git init` and `pre-commit install`; the hooks are local, nothing is cloned. |
| `format`, `format.ruff` | ruff rewrites files. |
| `lint`, `lint.ruff`, `lint.format`, `lint.pyproject`, `lint.pylint`, `lint.ty`, `lint.complexipy`, `lint.commitizen` | Every checker reads the tree; validate-pyproject carries its schemas. |
| `test`, `test.pytest`, `test.coverage` | pytest on the synced environment. |
| `test.view` | Opens a report in your browser; the page is local. |
| `grade`, `grade.pyscn`, `grade.pyscn-analyze`, `grade.pyscn-check`, `grade.pyscn-analyze-only`, `grade.pyscn-json-report` | pyscn ships its binary in its wheel. |
| `secure.sbom`, `secure.sbom-extract`, `secure.sbom-validate`, `secure.validate-overrides` | The SBOM is composed from the installed metadata and `uv.lock`; the schema is bundled. |
| `develop.pre-commit-install`, `develop.pre-commit`, `develop.pylock` | Local hooks; `uv export` reads the lock. |
| `document.serve` | Serves the site on localhost, rebuilding on change; the inventories `document.build` fetches are cached by then. |
| `preflight.staged` | The per-file checks above, on staged files. |
| `release.validate`, `release.bump`, `release.changelog`, `release.clean` | `release.validate` runs `git fetch origin`, which is the one exception: it reaches the git host. The others run commitizen on the tree. |
| `index.login`, `container.tag` in the open | Both say there is no fence and stop. |

## Commands that fetch

| Command | In the open | Behind the fence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `test.tox`, `preflight.tox` | *Index*, for an environment per interpreter in `env_list` (uv's cache serves what it has); *interpreters* the machine lacks. | The same, through the two variables; the netrc `index.login` wrote supplies the credentials. |
| `build`, `build.package` | *Index*, for the `uv_build` backend if the cache lacks it. | The same. |
| `document.build`, and `document` or `document.all`, which build first | `docs.python.org` and `typing-extensions.readthedocs.io`, for the two object inventories `properdocs.yml` names. | Unchanged, and unreachable from inside a network fence: drop or rehost the two `inventories` entries. |
| `secure.audit` | `pypi.org`, the advisory API, once per package; `--no-deps --disable-pip` keep it off the *index*. | Unchanged. Nothing proxies the advisory API; the audit needs egress to `pypi.org` or runs where it has it. |
| `develop.refresh-deps` | *Index*, `uv lock --upgrade`. | The same. |
| `develop.bump-uv` | `pypi.org`, for uv's releases; `ghcr.io`, for the image digest. | Unchanged and unreachable; the bump is a hand edit of the two pins. |
| `index.login`, `container.tag` | Nothing. | *Artifactory*{% if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}, and GitHub's token endpoint for the ID token first{% endif %}. |
| `container.build` | `ghcr.io`, the base image; *index* inside the build. | The base image from the mirror your `base-image` names, or `ghcr.io` if none; *index* through the credentials the builder stage is given. |
| `container.publish` | `container.build`, then {% if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}`ghcr.io`{% else %}`CI_REGISTRY`{% endif %} for the push and, with `--reuse`, the manifest check. | The same, plus *Artifactory* for the credentials. |
| `container.audit` | The container engine, locally; in a pipeline without one, {% if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}`ghcr.io`{% else %}`CI_REGISTRY`{% endif %} through the registry API. | Unchanged. |
| `preflight` | The union of `document.build`, `preflight.tox` and `build`; `--audit-dependencies` adds `secure.audit`. | The same union, through the fence. |

## Commands that publish

| Command | In the open | Behind the fence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `release` | `git push` to `origin`, then {% if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}`api.github.com`{% else %}the GitLab API at `CI_API_V4_URL`, or your instance by hand{% endif %} to open the {% if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}pull{% else %}merge{% endif %} request when a token is set. | Unchanged. |
| `release.dist` | `build` and `secure.audit`, above. | The same. |
| `release.attest` | Sigstore: `fulcio.sigstore.dev` for the signing certificate, `rekor.sigstore.dev` for the log, and the host's OIDC token endpoint. Skipped when `UV_PUBLISH_*` credentials are set. | Skipped: a fenced project publishes with credentials. |
| `release.publish` | `release.dist`, `release.attest`, then `upload.pypi.org`, with `pypi.org` first to mint the Trusted Publishing token. | `UV_PUBLISH_URL` instead of PyPI, and *Artifactory* for the credentials when only the URL is set. |
| `release.tag` | {% if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}`api.github.com`{% else %}the GitLab API{% endif %}, to create the tag and its release entry. | Unchanged. |
| `release.ship` | `git` on the local clone to detect the release, then `release.tag` and `release.publish`. | The same. |
{%- if git_hosting_service == 'github' %}
| `document.deploy-github` | `git push` of `gh-pages` to `origin`, then `api.github.com` to request the Pages build. | Unchanged. |
{%- endif %}

## The pipeline, per job
{% if git_hosting_service == 'gitlab' %}
Every job pulls its image from the registry named in the pipeline, and every job holds an ID
token nothing consumes unless the fence is set.

| Job | Reaches |
| --- | --- |
| `plan-deps-image` | `docker.io`, for `python:3-slim`; *index*, for `pip install uv` (`PIP_INDEX_URL` behind the fence); *Artifactory*, to mint the build's credentials when the fence is set. |
| `build-deps-image` | `gcr.io`, for the kaniko executor image; the base image, from `ghcr.io` or your mirror; *index* inside the build; `CI_REGISTRY`, for the push. |
| `preflight` | `CI_REGISTRY`, for the deps image and for `container.audit`; *Artifactory* for `index.login`; then everything `preflight` reaches above. |
| `secure` | `CI_REGISTRY`; *Artifactory* for `index.login`; `pypi.org` for the advisory API. |
| `publish` | `CI_REGISTRY`; *Artifactory* for `index.login` and the upload credentials; the GitLab API for the tag; Sigstore in the open; `upload.pypi.org` or `UV_PUBLISH_URL`. |
{% else %}
Every job fetches the actions it uses from `github.com`, and `setup-uv` downloads uv from
GitHub's releases wherever the deps image is not the job's container.

| Job | Workflow | Reaches |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `build-deps-image` | every workflow that needs the image | `github.com`, for the actions and uv; the base image, from `ghcr.io` or your mirror; *index* inside the build; `ghcr.io`, for the push; *Artifactory*, for the credentials when the fence is set. |
| `preflight` | `continuous-integration.yaml` | `ghcr.io`, for the deps image; *Artifactory* for `index.login`; then everything `preflight` reaches above. |
| `preflight-from-fork` | `continuous-integration.yaml` | `github.com` for the actions and uv; *index* and *interpreters* at job time, with no fence credentials; then `preflight`. |
| `secure`, `secure-from-fork` | `security-audit.yaml` | As the two above, then `pypi.org` for the advisory API. |
| `publish` | `publish.yaml` | `ghcr.io`; *Artifactory* for `index.login` and the upload credentials; `api.github.com` for the tag and the provenance attestation; Sigstore in the open; `upload.pypi.org` or `UV_PUBLISH_URL`. |
{%- if integrate_pages %}
| `deploy-docs` | `pages.yaml` | `ghcr.io`; `document.build`'s two inventory hosts; `git push` of `gh-pages`; `api.github.com` for the Pages build. |
{%- endif %}
