## Generation

`uvx copier copy` fetches copier from the *index* and the template from `github.com`, or from
a local clone when given a path. The render hook then asks `pypi.org` for uv's releases and
`ghcr.io` for the image digest, to stamp a fresh pin; both fall back to the committed pin and
say so, which is what happens behind a fence. It then runs `uvx uv lock`, which fetches uv
and resolves every package from the *index*, and `uvx ruff format`, which fetches ruff the
same way. A `uv lock` on a machine without the floor interpreter fetches that too.

## Not a command

The README badges are images on `img.shields.io` that the reader's browser fetches; nothing
in the project requests them. The links in the docs are links.
